  {
   "id": "q0dq5s8TLqEJ",
   "from": "Ben Goodrich",
   "author": "743bbacc59f4b25f",
   "date": "2015-02-06T15:34:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: normal diet with matrix input",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You want to do<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">to_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> normal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">to_vector</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y1_pred</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma_y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">);</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>That is the Stan equivalent of the R construct<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">y1_pred</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma_y</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> log </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Ben</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Friday, February 6, 2015 at 10:12:43 AM UTC-5, Andrew Gelman wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi, I tried this:\r\n<br>  y1 ~ normal(y1_pred, sigma_y);\r\n<br>in which y1 was a matrix, y1_pred was a matrix, and sigma_y is a scalar.  But it did not work.  Is that right?\r\n<br>A\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
